# 🛡️ Kavach-AI Ingestion Gateway & Swarm Daemon Test Suite
# REST API Specifications for Hackathon Judges & Developers
# Target Endpoint: http://localhost:8080 (Rust actix-web)

@host = http://localhost:8080
@apiVersion = api/v1
@contentType = application/json

###
# 1. Gateway Liveness Probe
# Verifies actix-web gateway status, runtime version, and configured interdiction budget.
GET {{host}}/{{apiVersion}}/health
Accept: {{contentType}}

###
# 2. Session Initialization (Hardware Gate)
# Starts a monitoring session. Validates browser metadata and checks for virtual camera drivers.
# 
# Note: Changing camera_device_label to "OBS Virtual Camera" or "v4l2loopback" will trigger 
# the instant virtual-camera driver block (HTTP 403 Forbidden).
#
# @name initSession
POST {{host}}/{{apiVersion}}/session/init
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: {{contentType}}

{
  "user_agent": "Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/120.0.0.0 Safari/537.36",
  "camera_device_label": "FaceTime HD Camera (Built-in)",
  "platform": "Win32"
}

###
# Extract the Session ID from the response above
@sessionId = {{initSession.response.body.session_id}}

###
# 3. Retrieve Current Threat Coordinates
# Pulls the fused threat index and per-agent telemetry scores from Redis cache.
# Real-time updates are pushed by the daemon swarm asynchronously.
GET {{host}}/{{apiVersion}}/session/{{sessionId}}/threat
Accept: {{contentType}}

###
# 4. Retrieve Full Session State
# Returns the entire session state metadata, device configurations, and signatures.
GET {{host}}/{{apiVersion}}/session/{{sessionId}}
Accept: {{contentType}}

###
# 5. Clean Session Termination
# Tears down state vectors, clear lists, and removes session context from Redis.
POST {{host}}/{{apiVersion}}/session/{{sessionId}}/close
Accept: {{contentType}}


# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WebSocket Streaming Simulation Instructions (RFC 6455)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Use an interactive WebSocket client (like wscat, websocat, or Postman) to test
# binary ingest streams:
#
# A. Audio Ingestion Stream:
#    ws://localhost:8080/api/v1/stream/audio?session_id={{sessionId}}
#    - Protocol: Binary
#    - Payload: Raw 16kHz mono PCM frames (Int16 samples, little-endian)
#    - Behavior: Automatically splits, buffers, and triggers the Phoneme/Hermes agents.
#
# B. Sensor Ingestion Stream:
#    ws://localhost:8080/api/v1/stream/sensor?session_id={{sessionId}}
#    - Protocol: Binary (Text fallback supported for debug)
#    - Format: JSON array representing "[gyro_x, gyro_y, gyro_z, touch_pressure, touch_x, touch_y]"
#    - Sample: [0.0012, -0.0025, 0.0049, 0.85, 320.0, 480.0]
#    - Behavior: Feeds high-pass filter + online Welford estimator. Trigger alerts if z-variance > 0.0045.


# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Outbound Mock Webhook Endpoints
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

###
# C. Mock Core Banking webhook (Receiver for Account Freeze commands)
# Fired by Nexus-Agent when circular mule loops are detected.
POST http://localhost:9001/api/freeze
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "action": "FREEZE_ACCOUNTS",
  "reason": "money_mule_circular_flow_detected",
  "session_id": "8fa8b301-4475-47e2-89cd-567a12b39df2",
  "accounts": ["501002300091", "501002300092", "501002300093"],
  "loop_depth": 3,
  "total_flow_inr": 125000.0,
  "timestamp": "2026-07-18T18:52:00Z",
  "legal_section": "Section 17 PMLA 2002"
}

###
# D. Mock Telecom SIP Gateway webhook (Call termination)
# Fired concurrently with account freezes to release victims from coercion.
POST http://localhost:9002/api/terminate
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "session_id": "8fa8b301-4475-47e2-89cd-567a12b39df2",
  "reason": "fraud_interdiction"
}
